{
  // The scanner's NeoPixel ring as a device: 35 pixels in a circle, standing
  // on the stage the scanner looks render into.
  //
  // Coordinates are literal, in the same space as the obelisk device (x is
  // across, y is up, the obelisk's floor at y=0): the ring is a circle of
  // radius 3.5 centred at (3.5, -4.5), so it hangs just below the obelisk -
  // its top pixel one unit under the floor - and spans the same width. That
  // is the point of it: a look that travels along y crosses the ring first
  // and then climbs the obelisk. Pixel 0 sits at the top of the circle,
  // numbered the way the physical ring runs; the centre and radius are
  // kRing* in src/relics/scanner/scanner_patterns.h, and the live game
  // writes the same circle inline - main-py/lib/jr_lib/eclipse_engine.py -
  // so the three have to agree.
  //
  // The viewer draws its picture from these same fields, which is why they
  // are a real circle and not a convenient line.
  //
  // Preview output: this device's frames only ever go to a screen - the real
  // ring is painted by the game out of the frame stream, never by a wire.

  "name": "scanner_ring",

  "coord_space": "literal",

  "output": {
    "type": "preview",
    "fps": 30
  },

